# Runtime data — never committed. Rebuildable from ingest, or irreplaceable and
# far too large for git (raw post archive + media). Back these up separately.
# Glob, not exact names: dated backups like traderlog.db.backup-pre-mock-purge
# carry the whole real corpus and were staged on 2026-08-23 because the pattern
# listed only the three exact filenames.
data/traderlog.db*
data/*.log
data/raw/
data/media/
data/bhavcopy/

# Local secrets + machine-specific config
config.yaml
.env

# Browser profiles for the X fetcher. These contain LIVE SESSION COOKIES for the
# user's logged-in X account — committing one would publish their session and
# hand anyone with repo access the ability to act as them on X.
#
# The glob is deliberately wide. On 2026-08-23 a `git add traderlog` staged
# `data/browser_profile_competing/Default/Network/Cookies` because the pattern
# was the exact directory `data/browser_profile/` and a later session had created
# a suffixed variant. It was caught in the pre-commit review and never committed.
# Match ANY profile-shaped directory, and belt-and-braces the cookie stores
# themselves wherever they appear.
data/browser_profile*/
**/Network/Cookies
**/Network/Cookies-journal
**/*.leveldb/
**/Local Storage/
**/Session Storage/

# Build output
ui/dist/
ui/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
